  "note": "Independent re-audit after 26d70dfa0d. Per-family LLST timers are still armed only in enterLLGRLocked (unchanged) at the GR deadline or immediately for omitted-GR families from onSessionDownPlan, whose only change adds preservedLLGRFams; restalePreservedLLGR arms no new timer for a family whose period runs, as RFC9494-4.2-9 requires. The new llgrFamilyActive reconnect guard sits after the timer is armed, so it cannot suppress the timer. Tagged roots unchanged and now run through the RIB's real answers: TestOnTimerExpired_WithLLGR, TestRFC9494RestartTimeThenLongLivedStaleTime and the three omitted-family positives require the per-family timer and its exact 1ns expiry; negatives TestOnSessionDown_ZeroGR_ZeroLLST, TestRFC9494BothTimesZeroRetainsNothing and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyWithoutLLSTIsRemoved require no timer and no retention for a zero or unexchanged LLST.",
